# Tests (PHPUnit)

## Layout

- **`tests/Feature/`** — HTTP tests against controllers (Auth, Character,
  Ruleset, LevelUp). Prefer `getJson` / `postJson` with
  `RefreshDatabase`.
- **`tests/Unit/`** — model/domain units (`Catalog/`, `CharacterSheet/`).
- **`tests/Integration/`** — concurrency and heavier cases
  (`composer test:concurrency`).

## Auth / Sanctum

- Auth is stateful SPA (cookie/session). Sanctum only starts the session when
  the request origin is listed in `SANCTUM_STATEFUL_DOMAINS`. Feature tests
  that hit authenticated routes must send an `Origin` header matching a
  stateful domain (see `ORIGIN_HEADERS` in `CharacterControllerTest`).
- Use `$this->actingAs($user)` for authenticated flows.

## Running

- Requires **PHP 8.4+** and a `.env` with a non-empty `APP_KEY`
  (`cp .env.example .env` then `php artisan key:generate` on a fresh
  checkout). Details: `AGENTS.md`.
- `composer test` runs PHPUnit via Artisan (`tests/Unit`, `tests/Feature`
  per `phpunit.xml`; in-memory SQLite).
- Before marking work done: also `./vendor/bin/pint --test`.

## Style

- One test class per controller/domain area, matching existing names
  (`CharacterControllerTest`, `RulesetControllerTest`, etc.).
- Prefer Laravel testing helpers over custom HTTP clients. Extend
  `Tests\TestCase`.
- When catalog or API contract shape changes, update Feature tests (and any
  shared helpers under `tests/Support/`) together.
